{"additions":186,"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTA5NDkz","is_bot":false,"login":"td72","name":"Kohei Hosokawa"},"body":"Closes #81\n\nStacked on #83 (base: `feat/issue-tree`) — reuses its tree builder. #83 and this PR form GitHub Stack #85 (`gh stack link 83 84`), which is what the demo shows.\n\n## Summary\nThe PR list nests PRs that belong to a **GitHub Stack** (the object `gh stack submit` / `link` / `sync` creates) bottom-to-top under the PR they build on. Nesting is driven only by stack membership — base branches are not inferred — so repositories without stacks keep a flat list.\n\n## Changes\n- `client::list_pr_stacks()`: one GraphQL query (`PullRequest.stack { number size }` / `stackEntry { position }`) for the open PRs, since `gh pr list --json` does not expose stacks. Merged into `GhPrListItem.stack` best-effort: if the query fails (older `gh`, API without stacks) the list is simply flat\n- `GhPrListItem::parent_number()`: the listed PR with the closest lower `position` in the same stack, so merged / closed entries missing from the open list are skipped over\n- Rows: the bottom PR of a stack shows ` stack #N`, nested rows show ` ← <base branch>` (dark gray, after the badges)\n- `baseRefName` is also fetched for that display; both new fields are `#[serde(default)]` so older disk caches still load\n- README (en/ja); `demo-github-pr.gif` re-recorded against stack #85\n- Unit test for parent resolution (gap in positions, other stack, unstacked PR)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01TreGn5Xh4PjDRv9Yo4QU4w\n","changedFiles":6,"comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-08-27T11:50:20Z","deletions":6,"headRefName":"feat/pr-stack","labels":[],"number":84,"reviewDecision":"","reviews":[{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLG6TMQ","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🟢 Approval recommended\n\nThe implementation matches the stated spec, is backward-compatible with existing caches, and includes unit test coverage for the new parent-resolution behavior.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Pull request overview</summary>\n\nThis PR enhances the GitHub PR list pane by rendering stacked PRs (where a PR’s base branch matches another open PR’s head branch) as a nested tree, improving readability for gh-stack-style workflows.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Fetches `baseRefName` from `gh pr list` and persists it in `GhPrListItem` with `#[serde(default)]` for backward-compatible disk cache loading.\n- Adds PR-specific parent resolution (`parent_number`) to drive nesting via the shared GitHub list tree builder.\n- Updates PR row rendering to append a dimmed `← <base>` suffix for nested PRs, and updates README docs (EN/JA); adds a unit test for parent selection.\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>File summaries</summary>\n\n| File | Description |\r\n| ---- | ----------- |\r\n| src/github/panes/pr_list.rs | Implements parent resolution for stacked PR nesting, renders base-branch suffix for nested rows, and adds a unit test. |\r\n| src/github/domain/types.rs | Adds `base_ref_name` to `GhPrListItem` with serde rename/default for cache compatibility. |\r\n| src/github/domain/client.rs | Extends `gh pr list --json` fields to include `baseRefName`. |\r\n| README.md | Documents stacked PR nesting behavior in the GitHub PR list. |\r\n| docs/README.ja.md | Japanese documentation update describing stacked PR nesting. |\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 6/6 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 0\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>\n\n---\n\n💡 <a href=\"/td72/vig/new/feat/issue-tree?filename=.github/skills/code-review/SKILL.md\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Add a `code-review` agent skill</a> or configure MCP servers for context-aware, tailored reviews. <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/how-tos/use-copilot-agents/request-a-code-review/use-code-review#mcp-servers-and-agent-skills\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Learn more in the docs.</a>","submittedAt":"2026-08-27T11:53:16Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"cf94f94585ae7a43a154b98fe03304ddd3b25e98"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLHChrg","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🟢 Approval recommended\n\nThe implementation matches the stated spec (best-effort stack fetch + position-based parent resolution) and includes both documentation updates and a focused unit test for the new nesting behavior.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 6/6 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 0 new\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>","submittedAt":"2026-08-27T12:07:36Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"71b23fae8878e79e6e2a18292f4c9387309d0ef8"}}],"state":"MERGED","statusCheckRollup":[{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-27T12:09:54Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33070592189/job/98511558500","name":"create-tag","startedAt":"2026-08-27T12:10:04Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Release"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-27T12:06:36Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33070244907/job/98510321334","name":"build (x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu, ubuntu-latest)","startedAt":"2026-08-27T12:05:20Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-27T12:05:46Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33070244823/job/98510318526","name":"lint","startedAt":"2026-08-27T12:05:19Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-27T12:06:08Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33070244907/